WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:16.530
Zann stared after the flizzes.

2
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:17.551
"What now?"

3
00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:20.273
"Should we use magic to find our way?"

4
00:00:20.513 --> 00:00:21.294
Venna suggested.

5
00:00:21.314 --> 00:00:23.935
"We might as well," Gliss said.

6
00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:26.938
"Wyssa used magic to create that knife just now."

7
00:00:27.658 --> 00:00:29.820
She rubbed her neck where the tree had grabbed her.

8
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.902
"That was minor magic," Wyssa said.

9
00:00:32.922 --> 00:00:37.847
"Any kind of searching or mapping spell would be—oh, hello."

10
00:00:39.028 --> 00:00:41.190
A Roodian servant was rushing toward them.

11
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.794
"The prince sent me to help you," he said in a hushed, urgent tone.

12
00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:49.537
"He realized you'd never find the queen and the other prisoners.

13
00:00:50.338 --> 00:00:53.861
Morb has put a Bewilderment spell over this whole place."

14
00:00:54.862 --> 00:00:55.563
"I knew it!"

15
00:00:56.003 --> 00:00:56.624
Wyssa muttered.

16
00:00:57.356 --> 00:01:01.099
"But we servants need to be able to find our way around to do our jobs."

17
00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.723
The Roodian cast a nervous look around as he showed them a small object.

18
00:01:06.743 --> 00:01:09.885
"That's why Morb gave each of us one of these."

19
00:01:10.746 --> 00:01:11.487
Perda gasped.

20
00:01:11.507 --> 00:01:12.687
"A talisman!

21
00:01:12.988 --> 00:01:15.650
Just like the one Morb used to control the trolls!"

22
00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.492
The Roodian handed the talisman to Wyssa.

23
00:01:18.512 --> 00:01:21.434
"It blocks the effects of the Bewilderment spell.

24
00:01:22.094 --> 00:01:23.996
Now you'll be able to find the prisoners' cell."

25
00:01:24.596 --> 00:01:27.299
He quickly told them the way and then scurried off.

26
00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.443
With Wyssa in the lead, Zann and the others followed the Roodian's directions.

27
00:01:33.204 --> 00:01:36.026
Soon they reached a large, dimly lit chamber.

28
00:01:36.807 --> 00:01:41.471
A haze of odorless smoke made it impossible to see more than a few steps ahead.

29
00:01:41.491 --> 00:01:43.333
"This should be the cell."

30
00:01:43.733 --> 00:01:44.714
Zann peered in.

31
00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.275
"Do you guys see anything?"

32
00:01:46.295 --> 00:01:51.580
"I can't see a thing through all this misty stuff," Gliss complained.

33
00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.044
Zann took a few careful steps forward, waving a hand to clear the haze.

34
00:01:57.064 --> 00:02:04.591
"I think I see something Zann's voice trailed off; his eyes widened in horror.

35
00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:06.833
A scatter beast was stepping out of the mist!

36
00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:08.695
Zann's heart raced.

37
00:02:09.035 --> 00:02:12.519
His head filled with memories of his last scatter beast encounter.

38
00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:15.281
He tried to speak, to warn his friends.

39
00:02:15.922 --> 00:02:17.984
But his voice seemed frozen in his throat.

40
00:02:19.244 --> 00:02:21.805
"Was that Roodian servant working for Morb?"

41
00:02:22.125 --> 00:02:23.105
he thought with a shudder.

42
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:25.786
"Did he send us straight into a trap?"

43
00:02:26.466 --> 00:02:31.187
The scatter beast paused, its tentacle waving lazily as it shambled closer.

44
00:02:31.207 --> 00:02:33.668
"No!" Venna shouted.

45
00:02:34.248 --> 00:02:39.990
But Zann barely noticed; all he could do was stare at the horrifying creature moving toward him.

46
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.610
Suddenly there was a loud squawk.

47
00:02:43.451 --> 00:02:47.472
Zing flew around Zann and the others, spitting fire and whistling urgently.

48
00:02:49.036 --> 00:02:49.976
"Zing, what are you doing?"

49
00:02:50.256 --> 00:02:53.397
Zann mumbled, barely feeling the burn of Zing's flames.

50
00:02:54.418 --> 00:02:55.198
"Save yourself."

51
00:02:56.038 --> 00:02:58.819
Zing let out a chirp of irritation and flew out of sight.

52
00:02:59.539 --> 00:03:04.321
For a moment Zann thought the dragon had taken his advice and escaped the way they'd come in.

53
00:03:05.481 --> 00:03:07.142
Then Zann heard another whistle.

54
00:03:07.862 --> 00:03:11.183
A second later something thumped into his back—hard.

55
00:03:11.963 --> 00:03:14.364
"Hey!" Zann blurted out as he stumbled forward.

56
00:03:14.984 --> 00:03:17.785
He was about to fall right on top of the scatter beast!

57
00:03:17.825 --> 00:03:22.246
"No—oof!" He landed hard on the stone floor of the chamber.

58
00:03:22.266 --> 00:03:24.127
"Huh?" Zann muttered.

59
00:03:24.867 --> 00:03:26.707
He couldn't see the scatter beast anymore.

60
00:03:27.908 --> 00:03:30.468
Zann leaped to his feet and backed up a few steps.

61
00:03:31.328 --> 00:03:35.870
Suddenly the scatter beast was there again, in the same spot where Zann had just fallen!

62
00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.410
Zing landed beside the scatter beast.

63
00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.731
The beast didn't seem to notice the dragon at all.

64
00:03:42.511 --> 00:03:44.332
Zann's wild heartbeat slowed.

65
00:03:45.292 --> 00:03:51.257
For the first time, he realized he wasn't feeling the pain and other crazy magical effects he'd felt

66
00:03:51.317 --> 00:03:51.958
in Fardark.

67
00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:55.240
The only thing immobilizing him was his fear.

68
00:03:56.021 --> 00:03:59.564
Taking a cautious step forward, Zann reached for the scatter beast.

69
00:04:00.325 --> 00:04:02.086
His hand passed right through it!

70
00:04:02.106 --> 00:04:03.847
"It's an illusion!"

71
00:04:04.108 --> 00:04:05.349
Zann shouted with relief.

72
00:04:06.149 --> 00:04:07.931
"The scatter beast isn't real!"

73
00:04:08.992 --> 00:04:09.812
He glanced around.

74
00:04:10.513 --> 00:04:15.401
Everyone else, except Zing, was staring straight ahead, looking terrified.

75
00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:18.383
"S-scatter beast?"

76
00:04:19.143 --> 00:04:21.885
Perda's eyes never left the blank spot right in front of her.

77
00:04:21.905 --> 00:04:25.728
"I'd be happy to see a scatter beast right now.

78
00:04:26.628 --> 00:04:30.311
Maybe it would scare away that huge swarm of tickle bugs!"

79
00:04:31.211 --> 00:04:31.992
"Tickle bugs?"

80
00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.473
Zann wrinkled his nose.

81
00:04:34.414 --> 00:04:39.077
Tickle bugs had ten legs and whirligig wings and liked to land on people.

82
00:04:39.777 --> 00:04:41.979
They were annoying, but they weren't scary.

83
00:04:42.359 --> 00:04:43.760
Well, except to Perda.

84
00:04:44.552 --> 00:04:48.435
Suddenly Zann remembered that Perda was terrified of the goofy insects.

85
00:04:48.835 --> 00:04:50.016
He'd once scared her with one.

86
00:04:50.036 --> 00:04:51.937
"I get it," he muttered.

87
00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:54.319
"Guys, none of this is real!"

88
00:04:54.539 --> 00:04:55.299
he said loudly.

89
00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:01.984
"Whatever you're seeing—tickle bugs, scatter beasts—they're just another one of Morb's spells.

90
00:05:03.145 --> 00:05:06.947
Somehow he's making us each see whatever scares us the most."

91
00:05:07.748 --> 00:05:08.949
Venna still didn't move.

92
00:05:08.969 --> 00:05:10.109
"Maybe you're right.

93
00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:13.732
But that cave hisser sure looks real to me.

94
00:05:14.516 --> 00:05:17.479
And everyone knows they don't like sudden movements."

95
00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.302
Zann sighed and then glanced at Zing.

96
00:05:21.322 --> 00:05:23.444
"Come on, little buddy.

97
00:05:23.724 --> 00:05:25.365
Let's show them."

98
00:05:25.385 --> 00:05:30.410
The two of them jumped in front of each person, revealing that whatever each was seeing wasn't real.

99
00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.291
"Thank goodness!"

100
00:05:32.672 --> 00:05:33.813
Gliss stumbled backward.

101
00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:37.576
"I was sure that thunder charger was going to eat me!"

102
00:05:38.356 --> 00:05:39.057
Darb nodded.

103
00:05:39.077 --> 00:05:42.300
"I thought I was about to fall into a deep, dark hole."

104
00:05:43.104 --> 00:05:44.085
"What did you see?"

105
00:05:44.265 --> 00:05:45.165
Perda asked Wyssa.

106
00:05:46.185 --> 00:05:47.766
Zann waited for Wyssa's answer.

107
00:05:48.506 --> 00:05:50.767
What could possibly terrify someone like her?

108
00:05:50.787 --> 00:05:52.688
"It's not important."

109
00:05:53.028 --> 00:05:55.870
Wyssa frowned, peering farther into the misty room.

110
00:05:55.890 --> 00:06:00.792
"This type of spell is very complex and difficult to cast.

111
00:06:01.552 --> 00:06:07.535
With so many real creatures roaming his lair, Morb would only bother to use a spell like this

112
00:06:07.615 --> 00:06:09.816
to protect something very important."

113
00:06:11.016 --> 00:06:12.937
She muttered a few words under her breath.

114
00:06:13.358 --> 00:06:14.698
Then she waved a hand.

115
00:06:14.718 --> 00:06:17.380
"Reveal!" she intoned.

116
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:22.823
The chamber seemed to melt away, revealing that it had all been an illusion.

117
00:06:22.843 --> 00:06:26.005
Zann and the others found themselves standing in an icy cave.

118
00:06:26.846 --> 00:06:29.287
A tiny woman was frozen in a block of ice.

119
00:06:30.108 --> 00:06:35.471
She was motionless, except for her eyes, which darted pleadingly from one person to the next.
